      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the LLM Provider**\n\nI've decided to use OpenAI as the external LLM provider for the `extract_json.py` script. The next step is to make this specific provider identifiable in the code.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Implementation**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the `extract_json.py` implementation. The plan is to create a function within the script that accepts text, calls the OpenAI API using a designated model like `gpt-3.5-turbo` to extract JSON, and returns that JSON. I'll need to remember to include both the `openai` import and model name for provider clarity.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820540604,
          "start": 1789820538677
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b99e0f35001XirByRCK5FQBZi",
      "message_id": "msg_0b99e0ab3001Sk2k1MPhn6d4Gf",
      "session_id": "ses_f4661f55affeemo53LyriP73EW",
      "time_created": 1789820538677,
      "time_updated": 1789820540604
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "kwDQ2W0JUZkcgsJQ",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import openai\nimport os\nimport json\n\ndef extract_json_from_text(text: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calls a hosted LLM (OpenAI) to extract structured JSON from text.\n\n    Args:\n        text: The input text from which to extract JSON.\n\n    Returns:\n        A dictionary representing the extracted JSON.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = openai.OpenAI(\n        api_key=os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"),\n    )\n\n    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n        model=\"gpt-3.5-turbo\", # OpenAI model identifier\n        response_format={ \"type\": \"json_object\" },\n        messages=[\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a helpful assistant designed to output JSON.\"},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": f\"Extract structured JSON from the following text: {text}\"}\n        ]\n    )\n    \n    # Assuming the LLM response is directly the JSON string\n    json_output = response.choices[0].message.content\n    return json.loads(json_output)\n\n",
            "filePath": "extract_json.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
